639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 532 0 R
/E (In the era of digital transformation, securing information systems has become a major strategic challenge for enterprises. Confronted with the constant evolution and increasing sophistication of cyber threats, traditional network architectures relying solely on perimeter protection are demonstrating their limitations. This final year project addresses this challenge by proposing the design, implementation, and validation of a highly secure, resilient, and scalable multi-site network architecture. The methodology relies on the modern paradigms of "Defense in Depth" and the "Zero Trust" model, ensuring that no network flow, whether internal or external, is implicitly trusted or authorized.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 532 0 R
/E (The technical solution, orchestrated around the open-source OPNsense firewall platform, is based on a strict micro-segmentation of environments \(LAN, DMZ, SRV, MGMT\) governed by the "Deny by Default" principle. To ensure business continuity, an advanced routing infrastructure was deployed, integrating Load Balancing and Failover mechanisms across Multi-WAN links. Furthermore, the confidentiality and integrity of inter-site communications are guaranteed by a cryptographic OpenVPN tunnel backed by a Public Key Infrastructure \(PKI\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 532 0 R
/E (Beyond routing and encryption, the architecture integrates upper-layer inspection mechanisms to proactively neutralize threats. A web proxy \(Squid\) provides application-level filtering and access control, while an Intrusion Detection and Prevention System \(Suricata IDS/IPS\) analyzes real-time traffic to actively block malicious behaviors. The entire infrastructure was rigorously validated through a comprehensive series of practical tests, including hardware failure simulations, Nmap intrusion attempts, and strict access policy verifications. These results prove the system's reliability, robustness, and full compliance with the stringent security requirements of a modern organization.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
642 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 532 0 R
/E (Keywords: Network Security, Zero Trust, Defense in Depth, Micro-segmentation, OPNsense, Site-to-Site VPN, Suricata IDS/IPS, High Availability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
